12:["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/50 overflow-hidden","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 p-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col items-center gap-1.5 pt-0.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-red-500"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500","children":4}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-0 flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-zinc-100","children":"Do the filling lines actually stop around 16:20, or do they keep running to about 19:00 with the output keyed in once at the end of the run?"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 rounded-lg border-l-2 border-emerald-500/50 bg-emerald-500/5 px-3 py-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80","children":"My guess"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 text-sm text-zinc-300","children":"They keep running. The 16:20-to-19:00 block is real production that nobody keys segment by segment. So the honest reading is a long day at about 47% efficiency, not a short day at 100%."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2 rounded-lg border-l-2 border-amber-500/60 bg-amber-500/5 px-3 py-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-400/80","children":"Changed since the rebuild"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 text-sm text-amber-100/90","children":"More important since the rebuild — v2 runs lines at 50% of rated. If they run past 16:20, that 50% means something else."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-1 text-xs text-zinc-500","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-zinc-600","children":"blocks:"}]," ","The entire capacity model, and whether the answer to a demand spike is a second shift or just better use of the day you already pay for."]}],"",""]}],""]}]]}]}]
13:["$","section","high",{"className":"mt-8","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-baseline justify-between mb-3","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-lg font-semibold","children":"High"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-zinc-500","children":[5," question","s"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","div","5",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-900/50 overflow-hidden","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-3 p-4","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col items-center gap-1.5 pt-0.5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-amber-500"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500","children":5}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"min-w-0 flex-1","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-zinc-100","children":"Is there a target for how long a bill may sit between the invoice and the truck? Today Oil's median is 2 days and the slowest one bill in ten waits more than 8 days, while the dock itself only takes about 2.5 hours."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 rounded-lg border-l-2 border-emerald-500/50 bg-emerald-500/5 px-3 py-2","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400/80","children":"My guess"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 text-sm text-zinc-300","children":"There is no target today and it has been drifting better on its own (4.85 days in June, 3.95 in July, 2.22 in August). I would set 24 hours as the goal — but it may be the customer's or the transporter's timing, not ours, in which case it is not a lever."}]]}],"",["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-2.5 flex flex-wrap gap-x-5 gap-y-1 text-xs text-zinc-500","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-zinc-600","children":"blocks:"}]," ","Knowing whether the ~145,000 L average standing pile is a problem to fix or just the cost of doing busines